Purpose:
The typewriter is a text editor that allows users to edit text files
on the command line. It supports typing of ASCII characters, 
backspace and enter, as well asundo and redoing of characters and 
new lines. The command menu allows users to save, exit, undo or 
redo. Files can be new or existing.

Acknowledgments:
The class chatbot.
I asked Ariel Jacobs to help test my program.
I went to office hours.
I consulted class lecture slides.

File List: 
 ActionStack.h
    ActionStacks store actions for undoing and redoing.

 ActionStack.cpp
    ActionStacks can be added to, popped from, and cleared.
    An action consists of a character, whether it was deleted,
    and its line and column.

 Editor.h
    The editor class contains most of the functionality for opening, editing,
    and saving a text file.

 Editor.cpp
    Users can add ascii characters, press enter and backspace to make
    new lines and delete characters, edit existing files or make
    new ones, save, and undo and redo changes.
    
 main.cpp
    Takes in the names of text file and optionally the logfile.
    If these parameters are correct, opens and runs the text editor.

 test logs:
    tests:
        the commands used to generate the test files below.

    enter_delete: 
        a keylogger test that includes enter and then delete
    enter_delete_M.text: 
        result of running enter_delete on my typewriter
    enter_delete_T.text: 
        result of running enter_delete on the example typewriter.

    newline_undo_redo
        a keylogger test that includes making, undoing, and redoing 
